f 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129079 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186368502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186368852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129179 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1045 "Tangent Planes to Level Surfaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186129892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1050 660.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129332 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "87e23de1-746c-5124-9751-bee5befcb28f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186127057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129596 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129596 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129596 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{y}-z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,e).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39528896-10e8-5126-bdec-f26e9bdcc487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129596 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j-k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,e) & ={e}^{1}\\text{ }i+(1){e}^{1}\\text{ }j-k \\\\  & =e\\,i+e\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨e,e,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129892 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129892 #edb/ref 1061 11201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129892 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "13f10d0e-ddd7-5833-b73f-b3f00ff7016a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129892 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129893 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129893 #edb/ref 1061 11204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129893 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6d9d3ca6-ae9b-5ac5-a35f-80fa6628ef2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129893 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130048 #edb/ref 1061 23124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130048 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f4dac68d-5f9a-5fba-b2c5-3ea5a9ec6475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130048 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130327 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we will learn how to compute the tangent plane to the level surface $f (x, y, z) = k,$ where $k$ is a constant, at some point $\\mathbf x_0 = (x_0, y_0, z_0).$ \n\nAs an example, consider the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = x^2 +y^2+z.\n$$\n\n \n\nSuppose that we wish to find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=  (1,1, 2).$ \n\nEvaluating $f$ at the point $(1,1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = (1)^2 +(1)^2+2 = 4.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the equation of our level surface is\n\n$$\nx^2 +y^2+z = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, to find the equation of the tangent plane to this surface at $(1,1,2),$ we can use the following result:\n\n  *Given a hypersurface $w = f(x,y,z)$ and a point $\\mathbf x_0 = (x_0,y_0,z_0)$ that lies in the domain of $f$, the gradient $\\nabla \\! f (\\mathbf x_0)$ is normal to the tangent plane of the level surface $f (x, y, z) = k$ at the point $\\mathbf x_0$*. \n\n![](images/11/1140e80fbb2efd684311cb7625e5b0be361d6fb951036253f57b9e51234de3ee.png)\n\n       \n\nWe can now find the equation of the tangent plane to our level surface.\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $\\mathbf x_0 = (1,1,2)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}\\,i+{f}_{y}\\,j+{f}_{z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+k \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2) & =2(1)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j+k \\\\  & =2\\text{ }i+2\\text{ }j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,  we write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle & = 0 \\[3pt]\n\\nabla f(1,1,2) \\cdot \\langle x-1, \\: y-1, \\: z-2 \\rangle & = 0 \\[3pt]\n\\langle 2,\\:2,\\:1\\rangle\\cdot \\langle x-1, y-1, z-2\\rangle &= 0\\[3pt]\n      2(x-1)+ 2(y-1) + (z-2) & =0\\\n      2x +2y +z -6&=0   \n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130327 #edb/ref 1065 2500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130327 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7f7db883-9d6e-5a67-97d4-20274467a1e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130327 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236008 #edb/ref 1080 "4x-y+2z-10=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236008 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236008 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d8438dc-a715-5c0c-aab2-6e47f02ae119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236650 #edb/ref 1080 "4x+3y+z+12=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236650 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236650 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85b07a3f-7374-5a9c-b7c1-947