] [17592186237932 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{z}^{2} & =6-z \\\\ xy{z}^{2}+z & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+z$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=6.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+(x{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+(2xyz+1)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,2) & =(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }i+(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }j+(2(1)(1)(2)+1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4j+5\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,4,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,4,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)+4(y-1)+5(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 4x+4y+5z-18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321465 #edb/ref 1080 "x-2y+2z-8=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321465 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321465 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28cd2801-6575-503c-8973-e5d77533e487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322054 #edb/ref 1080 "x-4y+z+6=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322054 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322054 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "740d2fc5-1db2-531b-9591-8ebbee71f486" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322509 #edb/ref 1080 "2x-y+z-4=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322509 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322509 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "adb3e2fe-6b96-5d2f-a240-7193b0f2a939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322659 #edb/ref 1080 "x+2y-2z-12=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322659 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322659 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2da99c8-1b83-5384-b154-4692549ce45c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322687 #edb/ref 1080 "x-2y+2z+4=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322687 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322687 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c69134c6-e59d-5120-8af3-0b8bb7f8b190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186322687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323391 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6e18b7a8-1caf-5bbf-be09-d1d09a6d4c0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323850 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323850 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36765" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323850 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323850 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the surface ${x}^{2}=-xyz.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,2,-2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323850 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c6c7087-87b2-59e1-b5dd-8db545cc6eaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323850 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =-xyz \\\\ {x}^{2}+xyz & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xyz$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,2,-2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x+yz)\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,2,-2) & =(2(4)+2(-2))\\text{ }i+4(-2)\\text{ }j+4(2)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-8j+8\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,-8,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,2,-2)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,-8,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)+(-8)(y-2)+8(z+2) & =0 \\\\ 4x-8y+8z+16 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+2z+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366815 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366815 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102704" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366815 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366815 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(\\frac{1}{2},3,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366815 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "baefe5d5-6705-561e-af37-627a61278732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366815 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(\\frac{1}{2},3,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =12x\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\frac{1}{2},3,2) & =12\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j+3(2)^{2}k \\\\  & =6\\,i-\\,j+12k \\\\  & =⟨6,-1,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{1}{2},3,2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y-3,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨6,-1,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y-3,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6(x-\\frac{1}{2})-(y-3)+12(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 6x-y+12z-24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186366817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366816 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ac4c269d-3ccc-505a-8b3b-1f9e614487fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366817 #edb/ref 1080 "6x-y+12z-24=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366817 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366817 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "193c9497-7ea6-5a1d-b9f5-a009ce93ca23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218636